# CropperSource

`CropperSource` renders a plain `<img>` for an image URL, with the right `crossorigin` attribute, and exposes the element through a bindable `ref`. None of the built-in croppers use it. It is a helper for custom components that need the image as a drawing source without displaying it the usual way:

- a custom cropper built with [`useAbstractCropper`](/docs/hooks/useAbstractCropper), whose background is not an `<img>`, can bind it to `refs.image` so that `getCanvas()` has something to draw from;
- a background that paints the image onto a `<canvas>` (for example with filters, as in the [Image Editor tutorial](/docs/tutorials/image-editor)) can draw from it once it has loaded.

## Usage

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import { CropperSource } from 'svelte-advanced-cropper';

	let { src }: { src: string } = $props();

	// Typed like CropperSource's `ref` prop. It always renders an `<img>`, which `draw` checks.
	let source: HTMLImageElement | HTMLCanvasElement | null = $state(null);
	let canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | undefined = $state();

	function draw() {
		const context = canvas?.getContext('2d');
		if (canvas && context && source instanceof HTMLImageElement) {
			canvas.width = source.naturalWidth;
			canvas.height = source.naturalHeight;
			context.filter = 'grayscale(1)';
			context.drawImage(source, 0, 0);
		}
	}
</script>

<canvas bind:this={canvas}></canvas>
<CropperSource bind:ref={source} {src} onload={draw} />
```

## Props

| Prop          | Type                                                | Default | Description                                                                                                         |
| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `src`         | `string` \| `null`                                   | —       | The image URL. Nothing is rendered without it, and the `<img>` is recreated whenever it changes.                    |
| `crossOrigin` | `'anonymous'` \| `'use-credentials'` \| `boolean`    | `true`  | The `crossorigin` attribute. `true` means `'anonymous'` and `false` leaves it off. Needed to draw cross-origin images onto a canvas. |
| `ref`         | `HTMLImageElement` \| `HTMLCanvasElement` \| `null`  | `null`  | **Bindable.** The rendered `<img>`, or `null` while there is none. The type also allows a canvas, as upstream's does. |
| ...rest       | `HTMLImgAttributes`                                 | —       | Any other `<img>` attribute or event handler, such as `alt`, `class` or `onload`.                                   |

The rest props are applied last, so a `class` you pass **replaces** the default `advanced-cropper-source` class instead of adding to it. That matches react-advanced-cropper. If you want the default styles too, include the class yourself: `class="advanced-cropper-source my-source"`.

## CSS classes

| Element | Classes                                                     |
| ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| Image   | `advanced-cropper-source` (unless you pass your own `class`) |

The base style hides the image, as it only serves as a source.
